 We study unsupervised domain adaptation (UDA) for speech emotion recognition (SER) from labeled non-verbal vocalizations (NVV) as source to unlabeled verbal speech (UVS) as target. We define the labeled source domain as a set of NVV waveforms paired with emotion labels:
𝒟S={(xiS,yi)}i=1NS,yi∈{1,…,C}\mathcal{D}_{S}=\{(x_{i}^{S},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N_{S}},\quad y_{i}\in\{1,\dots,C\}
where xiSx_{i}^{S} is a NVV waveform (e.g., laugh/cry/sigh) and yiy_{i} is its emotion label. We define the unlabeled target domain as a set of UVS waveforms:
𝒟T={xjT}j=1NT\mathcal{D}_{T}=\{x_{j}^{T}\}_{j=1}^{N_{T}}
where xjTx_{j}^{T} is a UVS waveform containing lexical content, and we do not use transcripts or emotion labels during target training.

